  @input:provider-candidate-completeness-request
  @input-contract:provider-candidate-completeness-request.v1
  @event:qualify-provider-candidate-completeness
  @event-authority:qualify-provider-candidate-completeness.v1
  @outcome:provider-candidate-completeness-receipt
  @outcome-contract:provider-candidate-completeness-receipt.v1
  @outcome-variants:CONFORMS|NOT_APPLICABLE|HELD
  @outcome-terminal
  Scenario: Return one exact provider completeness disposition
    Given one request carrying a frozen provider-candidate generation, canonical blueprint candidate, provider-slot requirement set, provider-candidate evidence set, coverage inputs, policy, and claimed digests
    When every digest and generation is validated, provider applicability is classified, every expected provider slot and closed-profile member is qualified, coverage is closed, and replay is compared
    Then CONFORMS is returned only with zero findings for every provider slot, NOT_APPLICABLE is returned only with independent provider-free proof, and every missing divergent stale ambiguous unresolved or non-reproducible obligation returns HELD with its exact policy finding

  @scenario:validate-provider-candidate-generation
  @input:provider-candidate-completeness-request
  @input-contract:provider-candidate-completeness-request.v1
  @event:validate-provider-candidate-generation
  @event-authority:validate-provider-candidate-generation.v1
  @outcome:provider-candidate-generation-validation
  @outcome-contract:provider-candidate-qualification-disposition.v1
  Scenario: Reject stale divergent or foreign-generation provider evidence
    Given one request whose generation binds exact feature blueprint estate policy provider-source contract target conformance and query-catalog bytes
    When every claimed digest is recomputed and every evidence product is resolved
    Then a matching generation is eligible for qualification, while stale foreign missing or digest-divergent evidence returns its exact finding without consuming the evidence as current truth

  @scenario:classify-provider-applicability
  @input:provider-candidate-completeness-request
  @input-contract:provider-candidate-completeness-request.v1
  @event:classify-provider-applicability
  @event-authority:classify-provider-applicability.v1
  @outcome:provider-applicability-disposition
  @outcome-contract:provider-candidate-qualification-disposition.v1
  Scenario: Prove provider applicability rather than defaulting by omission
    Given one exact blueprint candidate and independently derived provider-slot effect-boundary and provider-delegating dependency inventories
    When their expected provider obligations are compared
    Then a provider-bearing candidate is REQUIRED, a provider-free candidate is NOT_APPLICABLE only when every inventory proves zero provider obligations, and silence mismatch or an unmapped provider-requiring boundary returns PROVIDER_NOT_APPLICABLE_UNPROVEN or PROVIDER_CANDIDATE_COVERAGE_INCOMPLETE

  @scenario:qualify-provider-slot-evidence
  @input:provider-slot-qualification-request
  @input-contract:provider-slot-qualification-request.v1
  @event:qualify-provider-slot-evidence
  @event-authority:qualify-provider-slot-evidence.v1
  @outcome:provider-slot-evidence-disposition
  @outcome-contract:provider-candidate-qualification-disposition.v1
  Scenario: Require complete attributable evidence for one provider slot
    Given one provider-slot requirement and its candidate evidence carrying shape observation published semantics scenario-fit hypothesis precedent native and canonical contracts effects authorization conformance targets and source receipts
    When completeness attribution freshness and exact circuit-cell applicability are evaluated
    Then the slot closes only when every required class and field has a supported disposition, explicit NONE_FOUND precedent remains distinct from missing precedent, and every absent unresolved stale or unattributed item returns its exact finding

  @scenario:qualify-provider-selection
  @input:provider-slot-selection-request
  @input-contract:provider-slot-selection-request.v1
  @event:qualify-provider-selection
  @event-authority:qualify-provider-selection.v1
  @outcome:provider-slot-selection-disposition
  @outcome-contract:provider-candidate-qualification-disposition.v1
  Scenario: Require one exact binding or one completely closed profile
    Given one provider slot with one or more attributed candidates and a claimed selection mode
    When exact binding cardinality or closed-profile membership is evaluated
    Then an exact binding closes only with one authorized selected operation, a closed profile closes only when every eligible member independently satisfies the same obligation, and multiple undispositioned candidates model selection or an incomplete member returns its exact finding

  @scenario:qualify-provider-mapping-and-effects
  @input:provider-slot-realization-request
  @input-contract:provider-slot-realization-request.v1
  @event:qualify-provider-mapping-and-effects
  @event-authority:qualify-provider-mapping-and-effects.v1
  @outcome:provider-slot-realization-disposition
  @outcome-contract:provider-candidate-qualification-disposition.v1
  Scenario: Reject shape-only mappings and unproven effect absence
    Given one provider operation with native and canonical contracts claimed mapping mechanics effect posture authorization targets and conformance evidence
    When semantic type encoding unit admitted-mechanic target-support effect and authorization closure are evaluated
    Then a mapping closes only through admitted target-realized mechanics, effect absence closes only through attributable semantics classification and applicable falsification evidence, and shape-only mapping none-observed purity or an unbound target effect authorization or conformance returns its exact finding

  @scenario:preserve-provider-inference-as-testimony
  @input:provider-candidate-evidence-set
  @input-contract:provider-candidate-evidence-set.v1
  @event:preserve-provider-inference-as-testimony
  @event-authority:preserve-provider-inference-as-testimony.v1
  @outcome:provider-inference-authority-disposition
  @outcome-contract:provider-candidate-qualification-disposition.v1
  Scenario: Prevent affinity frequency or model confidence from becoming authority
    Given provider candidates carrying observed shapes documentation scenario affinities precedent frequencies model rationale or confidence values
    When their authority classes and claimed selection basis are evaluated
    Then every value remains attributed to its evidence class, none may select approve admit or authorize a provider, and any inference used as a binding or pass signal returns PROVIDER_INFERENCE_ESCAPED

  @scenario:preserve-carrier-provider-blackout
  @input:carrier-provider-qualification-request
  @input-contract:carrier-provider-qualification-request.v1
  @event:preserve-carrier-provider-blackout
  @event-authority:preserve-carrier-provider-blackout.v1
  @outcome:carrier-provider-blackout-disposition
  @outcome-contract:provider-candidate-qualification-disposition.v1
  Scenario: Resolve immutable provider evidence without completing carrier meaning
    Given one extracted graph and blackout receipt bound to an exact complete semantic-carrier digest whose graph carries provider meaning selection or closed profile canonical contracts and immutable evidence references
    When provider completeness is qualified from the graph and referenced evidence
    Then exact referenced evidence may be resolved without receiving reading or changing the carrier bytes, while any attempt to invent select repair or complete missing provider meaning returns PROVIDER_INFERENCE_ESCAPED and HELD with no AUTHOR fallback

  @scenario:close-provider-candidate-coverage
  @input:provider-candidate-coverage-inputs
  @input-contract:provider-candidate-coverage-inputs.v1
  @event:close-provider-candidate-coverage
  @event-authority:close-provider-candidate-coverage.v1
  @outcome:provider-candidate-coverage-ledger
  @outcome-contract:provider-candidate-coverage-ledger.v1
  Scenario: Prove expected versus verified provider coverage
    Given the independently derived expected provider-slot set and every validated slot and closed-profile-member disposition for one blueprint candidate
    When canonical coverage rows are ordered and expected observed selected closed and held cardinalities are compared
    Then every expected slot has exactly one row retaining all member findings, complete verified cardinality may close, and missing duplicate foreign or unresolved work returns PROVIDER_CANDIDATE_COVERAGE_INCOMPLETE rather than zero findings

  @scenario:replay-provider-candidate-qualification
  @input:provider-candidate-completeness-request
  @input-contract:provider-candidate-completeness-request.v1
  @event:replay-provider-candidate-qualification
  @event-authority:replay-provider-candidate-qualification.v1
  @outcome:provider-candidate-replay-disposition
  @outcome-contract:provider-candidate-qualification-disposition.v1
  Scenario: Require byte-identical replay without self-issued correctness
    Given two independent qualifications over the same frozen request bytes and policy identity
    When coverage rows findings dispositions and receipt digests are recomputed and canonically compared
    Then byte-identical products establish deterministic replay without claiming semantic correctness, and any difference returns PROVIDER_CANDIDATE_REPLAY_DIVERGED and HELD
